# Walkthrough: Product Search Semantic Upgrade

I have completed a rigorous semantic upgrade of the `product_search` intent system. This upgrade moves the system from deterministic keyword matching toward a more robust, scenario-driven model aligned with African Style Simple English.

## Key Changes

### 1. Scenario-Driven Bench Expansion
- **20 Situational Scenarios**: Generated scenarios covering specific needs, categories, budget, occasions, restocking, etc.
- **Relocation of Non-Search Variations**: Moved ~40 variations to more appropriate intents:
    - `get_product_details` (9 variations)
    - `vendor_info` (8 variations)
    - `product_compare` (2 variations)
    - `get_advice` (17 variations)
    - `browse_collection` (3 variations)
    - `add_to_cart` (3 variations)
- **Bench Upgrade**: Added 20 new variations in **African Style Simple English** to ensure 100% coverage of the 20 scenarios.

### 2. Configuration Cleanup
- **Pruning Synonyms**: Cleaned up [product_search.js](file:///C:/Users/chatz/Downloads/eCommerce/be3_ai/src/services/intentResolver/config/intents/product_search.js) by removing generic greeting synonyms ('hi', 'hello', 'hey', etc.) that belonged to the `conversation` intent. This prevents intent collisions and ensures cleaner transitions.

## Verification
- **Test cases generated**: Created a comprehensive set of test cases in [verification_test_cases.md](file:///C:/Users/chatz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/434fa0f1-1d5d-4ea9-ba51-c96a4d6056ed/verification_test_cases.md) for the user to verify against the transformer service.

